<article class="env-lemma" id="0GK1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GK1">Lemma <span data-tag="0GK1">63.12.3</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a separated scheme of finite type over a field $k$. If $\mathcal{F}$ is a torsion abelian sheaf, then the abelian group $H^0_ c(X, \mathcal{F})$ defined in Definition <a href="/tag/0F72" data-tag="0F72">63.3.7</a> agrees with the abelian group $H^0_ c(X, \mathcal{F})$ defined in Definition <a href="/tag/0GJZ" data-tag="0GJZ">63.12.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a compactification $j : X \to \overline{X}$ over $k$. In both cases the group is defined as $H^0(\overline{X}, j_!\mathcal{F})$. This is true for the first version by Lemma <a href="/tag/0F75" data-tag="0F75">63.3.10</a> and for the second version by construction. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>